Error: Jet.ValueNotSendable: `pool` can't cross into a task because `Pool` isn't sendable
  --> Tests/UI/Ownership/local_type_stays_on_its_thread.jet:13:18
    |
 12 |     worker: task {
    |                  ^
 Why: `Pool` is declared `#Local`, so its values stay on the thread that made them; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: Give the task plain owned data, or rebuild the value as an owned copy before spawning
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ValueNotSendable

